1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,268
Today is October 07, 2026.

3
00:00:07,268 --> 00:00:12,893
Overnight, the S&P 500 and the Nasdaq surged to fresh all-time records.

4
00:00:12,893 --> 00:00:16,447
Treasury yields eased while crude oil retreated.

5
00:00:16,447 --> 00:00:20,000
Risk appetite roared back into global equities.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,400
The S&P 500 closed up fifty-eight basis points.

7
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:28,432
The tech-heavy Nasdaq added forty-five basis points.

8
00:00:28,432 --> 00:00:33,015
Meanwhile, the Russell 2000 fell zero point six percent.

9
00:00:33,015 --> 00:00:37,206
The Nasdaq to Russell ratio hit a record ten point eight eight.

10
00:00:37,206 --> 00:00:41,643
Capital is crowding exclusively into mega-cap balance sheets.

11
00:00:41,643 --> 00:00:48,800
On the macro front, a solid fifty-eight billion dollar three-year Treasury auction relieved near-term supply fears.

12
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:53,383
The Fed rate cut path remains constrained by lingering deficits.

13
00:00:53,383 --> 00:00:57,844
August trade deficit widened to one hundred and five billion dollars.

14
00:00:57,844 --> 00:01:01,679
Surging semiconductor imports drove this expansion.

15
00:01:01,679 --> 00:01:06,349
Prominent bears claim markets are entering a late-stage denial phase.

16
00:01:06,349 --> 00:01:09,915
However, market internals tell a different story.

17
00:01:09,915 --> 00:01:15,123
The S&P broke cleanly above the critical seventy-eight hundred resistance level.

18
00:01:15,123 --> 00:01:18,738
That move triggered massive systematic short-covering.

19
00:01:18,738 --> 00:01:22,476
Fear and greed gauges sit near neutral territory.

20
00:01:22,476 --> 00:01:27,978
We are witnessing left-side momentum expansion, not an exhausted right-side rollover.

21
00:01:27,978 --> 00:01:31,091
Key technical watchpoints remain clear.

22
00:01:31,091 --> 00:01:34,547
Seventy-eight hundred serves as the primary pivot.

23
00:01:34,547 --> 00:01:38,334
A break below seventy-eight hundred warns of a bull trap.

24
00:01:38,334 --> 00:01:42,623
Holding above opens the door to seventy-nine hundred and eight thousand.

25
00:01:42,623 --> 00:01:48,407
Nasdaq futures must defend seven hundred and fifty-nine to target seven hundred and seventy-eight.

26
00:01:48,407 --> 00:01:54,228
Across industry flows, capital is aggressively rotating into AI infrastructure.

27
00:01:54,228 --> 00:02:00,050
Big tech capital expenditures are fueling unprecedented demand for clean baseload power.

28
00:02:00,050 --> 00:02:07,611
Nuclear provider Constellation Energy soared twelve percent following a landmark twenty-year power purchase agreement with Alphabet.

29
00:02:07,611 --> 00:02:12,317
Alphabet secured thirty-six hundred megawatts of dedicated capacity.

30
00:02:12,317 --> 00:02:18,371
This mirrors Amazon's nuclear strategy, sending utility valuations to fresh peaks.

31
00:02:18,371 --> 00:02:21,949
AI power demand is no longer theoretical.

32
00:02:21,949 --> 00:02:28,309
Energy Information Administration forecasts show record power consumption across data centers this year.

33
00:02:28,309 --> 00:02:32,023
Hardware supply chains show tactical divergence.

34
00:02:32,023 --> 00:02:39,241
Storage leaders like Seagate tumbled nine percent on aggressive acquisition spending rumors and Toshiba head headwinds.

35
00:02:39,241 --> 00:02:44,302
Conversely, custom silicon and optical networking gained strong momentum.

36
00:02:44,302 --> 00:02:51,312
Marvell popped nearly six percent after boosting fiscal twenty-thirty-one revenue guidance to ninety billion dollars.

37
00:02:51,312 --> 00:02:57,476
AMD surged three percent after confirming sustained enterprise server processor shortages.

38
00:02:57,476 --> 00:03:01,030
Turning to key pivotal equities for your trading radar.

39
00:03:01,030 --> 00:03:03,285
First, Nvidia.

40
00:03:03,285 --> 00:03:09,425
The semiconductor titan is knocking on a unprecedented six trillion dollar market cap valuation.

41
00:03:09,425 --> 00:03:14,486
Year-to-date market capitalization expansion exceeded one trillion dollars.

42
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:20,540
Remarkable forward earnings power keeps valuation multiples near ten-year historical medians.

43
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:24,204
Yet institutional concentration risk is extreme.

44
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:28,787
Nvidia effectively acts as the equity market's ultimate put option.

45
00:03:28,787 --> 00:03:32,059
Second, Advanced Micro Devices.

46
00:03:32,059 --> 00:03:36,300
The stock hit record highs at six hundred and fifty-eight dollars.

47
00:03:36,300 --> 00:03:43,432
Chief Executive Lisa Su reaffirmed that accelerator and server CPU demand far outstrips current supply.

48
00:03:43,432 --> 00:03:49,596
AI agent frameworks are driving massive CPU compute loads alongside GPUs.

49
00:03:49,596 --> 00:03:53,273
Wall Street targets pushed toward eight hundred dollars.

50
00:03:53,273 --> 00:03:59,179
Maintain trailing stops near six hundred and twenty dollars to safeguard recent breakout gains.

51
00:03:59,179 --> 00:04:03,248
Third, Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company.

52
00:04:03,248 --> 00:04:09,253
Shares rallied on reports of direct foundry collaboration with Tesla on the TerraFab project.

53
00:04:09,253 --> 00:04:15,675
Industry channel checks assign an eighty percent probability to this joint Texas manufacturing footprint.

54
00:04:15,675 --> 00:04:22,599
With Nvidia projecting seventy percent top-line expansion, TSMC commands complete pricing power.

55
00:04:22,599 --> 00:04:27,059
Downside risk centers on geopolitical supply chain friction.

56
00:04:27,059 --> 00:04:31,067
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

57
00:04:31,067 --> 00:04:35,233
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
